4. THE SAFETY PROPERTY — three deletion guards — PASS (the hardest criterion)
   Exactly one call to `deps.removeSrc` exists (handlers.go:696). The only path
   to it is the tail of importOneFile (handlers.go:616-705), and it requires
   ALL THREE guards to have held:
     Guard A (write succeeded): deps.write(destPath,data,0644) returned nil
       at :672; a non-nil error returns "rejected" at :673 before the readback.
     Guard B (readback matched): deps.readBack(destPath) returned no error
       (:679) AND len(back)==len(data) (:683); a short readback returns
       "rejected" at :684, a readback error at :681.
     Guard C (direct child): srcPath was Lstat'd as a regular non-symlink file
       (:641-650) and isDirectChild(cfg.ImportDirectory, srcPath) returned true
       (:651); both sides go through filepath.EvalSymlinks so a symlinked
       import folder still matches while anything reached by leaving it does
       not (handlers.go:713-723).
   `deleteSource` (line 586) is a fourth, explicit toggle; with it false the
   function returns at :690 before removeSrc.
   Skipped/rejected files NEVER reach line 696:
     - Step 1 name validation (:621-624) and non-CSV check (:628-630) run
       before any filesystem call — traversal/separator names rejected without
       touching the FS.
     - Step 2 not-found/symlink/non-regular/non-child (:642-653) returns before
       the write.
     - Step 3 collision (:661-662) and destination-stat error (:663-665)
       return before the write.
   This is verified by tests that stage each guard failing in isolation and
   assert `removed == false` and the source survives:
     TestImportOneFile_ShortReadbackNeverDeletes (handlers_test.go:2598) —
       readback returns importCSV[:10], asserts removed false, source exists.
     TestImportOneFile_ReadbackErrorNeverDeletes (:2625) — readback errors,
       same assertions.
     TestImportOneFile_SubdirectoryEntryNeverDeletes (:2647) — non-direct-child,
       both "sub/nested.csv" and "nested.csv" spellings rejected, removed false.
     TestImportOneFile_WriteFailureNeverDeletes (:2598 region) — write fails,
       removed false.
   The mixed-batch test (TestHandleImport_MixedBatchDeletesOnlyImported,
   :2732) seeds good.csv + dupe.csv (collision) + notes.txt (non-CSV) +
   ../escape.csv (traversal) in one POST with delete_source=true and asserts
   only good.csv's source is deleted; collide/txt/escape sources survive. All
   26 import tests pass under `go test ./internal/handlers/explorer/ -run
   'Import|IsDirectChild' -v`.

